From 1d7fbaefe1c45c82e6869646b2d7963a2ee3c0f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qualcomm-toolbox <169756160+qcom-toolbox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:25:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] umi: /dev/sweet-audio feeds the ADSP speaker stream from iOS
 (sweetaudio=1)

With sweetaudio=1 the test tone's stream (ASM session 1 -> ADM NULL COPP ->
TERT_MI2S_RX SD1) opens once the port runs and is fed from userland:
write() takes S16LE stereo 48 kHz frames into 20 ms periods of the shared
buffer (never blocks, at most 160 ms ahead, EAGAIN when full, ENXIO before
the stream), the GLINK loop sends full periods as ASM writes and frees them
on WRITE_DONE, a stale half period goes out padded. Both amps stay enabled
while it serves. ioctls: Q16 gain, stats, and a log line for the HAL
plug-in's bring-up trace; opens and the first write are logged.

On the phone, with SweetAudio.driver (phone/sweet-audio) and Apple's
VirtualAudio.plugin in place, iOS's ringtones play from the speaker.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
